      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day in many guidelines). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily** or another typical starting dose. Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily and increased slowly.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check it with your resident or attending. I'll enter the order once it's confirmed."
      }
