       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum daily dose. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) justifies it, and I can't think of a clinical reason for it. Your confirmation tells me the order is intentional, but it doesn't make the dose safe.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Dose check with your supervisor.** Review the order with your resident, attending, or a pharmacist. If they want a dose above the labeled maximum, they should enter it themselves or tell you the reason explicitly.\n- **A corrected dose.** I can enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). I can also enter a lower dose or a titration schedule if you prefer.\n- **A possible typo.** If you meant 1,700 mg/day total, I can enter 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
